// A trailing if is a condition only when a whole expression ends the line,
// like the lexer reads it (Lexer.isConditionUntilLineEnd).

beat Start
  Tell me if it is true.
//^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted
//        ^^ - keyword.control
  I would, if not now.
//^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted
//            ^^^ - keyword.control
  Tell me if you and I agree.
//^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted
//               ^^^ - keyword.control
  Run if (really) you must.
//^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted
  Stop if you must. Now
//^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted
  Shown if ok
//^^^^^ string.unquoted
//      ^^ keyword.control
//         ^^ variable.other
  Hidden if not ok
//^^^^^^ string.unquoted
//       ^^ keyword.control
//          ^^^ keyword.control
//              ^^ variable.other
  Also if mood is "angry"
//^^^^ string.unquoted
//        ^^^^ variable.other
//             ^^ keyword.control
//                ^^^^^^^ string.quoted.double
  Also if mood is not "angry"
//             ^^ keyword.control
//                ^^^ keyword.control
//                    ^^^^^^^ string.quoted.double
  Both if ok and not missing
//^^^^ string.unquoted
//           ^^^ keyword.control
